 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-201", "title": "Approval leg of the spec-to-build loop: record the approved task-packet digest and trace on the canonical board row so the approved bytes are tamper-evidently bound", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "7f7229e1792eac72e7b7a89bf600ab5ca0d65f9a44ca9154606da2a65de4b5bc"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "auger spec judge-packet refuses unless the canonical row carries the approved packet and the marker resolves to this row, this task and its own obligations; the approval ledger (spec plan-approve --digest) already binds decisions to the current digest. The missing piece is the write path: run spec task-packet, approve the digest into the ledger, and record packet id, digest, trace and ledger path on the canonical row via boardctl update - no hand-serialized JSONL edits. docs/XML-SPEC-COVERAGE.md lists approval-bound board write (R9) as designed only. This is the leg that makes worker and judge see the same bytes.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-22T15:38:16+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-22T15:38:16+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["spec", "boardctl", "gitreins"], "depends_on": ["AUG-200"], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": ["auger-spec-loop-filing-2026-11-22"], "type": "feat", "acceptance_criteria": "AC1: a writer path that for a spec-bearing row runs auger spec task-packet SPECSROOT --task TASKID, records the approval via auger spec plan-approve --plan PLANID --digest DIGEST --approver NAME --ledger DIR, and writes packet id, digest, trace and ledger path onto the canonical board row with boardctl update (style-preserving one-line physical diff). AC2: after the write, auger spec judge-packet --plan PLANID --row ROWID --board .coding-hermes/board succeeds (exit 0, packet path on stdout) against the real board, proving the row carries what judge intake requires. AC3: tamper evidence proven: change one block in the spec corpus after approval and judge-packet refuses with a typed refusal naming the offending ids; the row digest cannot be silently refreshed - a new ledger decision is required. AC4: proven end-to-end on one real row in this repo with the row id, packet digest and ledger record named in the evidence. AC5: no full-file re-serialization of tasks.jsonl (one removed plus one added physical line for the touched row); boardctl validate error count stays at the pre-write baseline of 0.", "worker_summary": null, "completed_at": null}
